  "question": {
    "text": "An electromagnetic wave with frequency $\\omega$ and wavelength $\\lambda$ travels in the $+y$ direction. Its magnetic field is along $+x$-axis. The vector equation for the associated electric field (of amplitude $E_0$ ) is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Oy5SZ",
      "text": "\n$\\vec{E}=-E_0 \\cos \\left(\\omega t+\\frac{2 \\pi}{\\lambda} y\\right) \\hat{x}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "rpOuC",
      "text": "\n$\\vec{E}=E_0 \\cos \\left(\\omega t-\\frac{2 \\pi}{\\lambda} y\\right) \\hat{x}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "InXHs",
      "text": "\n$\\vec{E}=E_0 \\cos \\left(\\omega t-\\frac{2 \\pi}{\\lambda} y\\right) \\hat{z}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ytU6X",
      "text": "\n$\\vec{E}=-E_0 \\cos \\left(\\omega t+\\frac{2 \\pi}{\\lambda} y\\right) \\hat{z}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In an electromagnetic wave electric field and magnetic field are perpendicular to the direction of propagation of wave. The vector equation for the electric field is\n$$\n\\vec{E}=E_0 \\cos \\left(\\omega t-\\frac{2 \\pi}{\\lambda} y\\right) \\hat{z}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
